  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "6b05ad4d-936f-48d1-befa-46a299907468"],
 "."
}], "Usage",
 CellID->1011,ExpressionUUID->"d05337df-52b6-4667-9262-771ac0898b51"],

Cell["\<\
MakeArray[expr] recognises a line element by the CircleTimes in it and a \
differential form by the Wedge, and gives the corresponding array of \
components.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1012,ExpressionUUID->"672435ba-fb18-4a14-875b-1e90458bee07"],

Cell["\<\
The chart is deduced from the coordinate differentials appearing in expr, so \
it need not be supplied.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1013,ExpressionUUID->"5a63a81e-2f89-4187-bb7a-a964df29d4d9"],

Cell["\<\
For a line element the result is symmetrised; for a form of degree n it is \
the totally antisymmetric array of rank n.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1014,ExpressionUUID->"faf69764-df46-4b8b-9931-6be361015507"],

Cell["MakeArray is the inverse of MakeMetric and of MakeForm.", "Notes",
 CellID->1015,ExpressionUUID->"69e85268-42cd-4100-ba01-7aee9011f6e7"],

Cell["\<\
It issues MakeArray::nodiffs if there are no Diff's to read a chart from, and \
MakeArray::nochart if none of the coordinates found belongs to a chart.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1016,ExpressionUUID->"6e2daacc-293b-4a6d-93ad-74ab73ca9068"],

Cell["\<\
It is the usual first step of a metric Chain, as MakeArray[$self[$metric, gg, \
Expression]].\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1017,ExpressionUUID->"1168c91f-8ba7-4c0a-bf08-14c0dbd8339a"]
}, Open  ]],

